# The published package is defined by the `files` allowlist in package.json
# (dist + README + LICENSE). This .npmignore exists on purpose: without it, npm
# falls back to .gitignore, whose `dist/` entry would strip the built plugin
# out of the tarball. Keeping this file empty of a `dist` rule guarantees the
# built manifest ships.
#
# Internal dev artifacts (ISA.md, Plans/, tests/, src/) are excluded by the
# allowlist, so they are never published — but list them here too as defense in
# depth in case the allowlist is ever loosened.
ISA.md
Plans/
tests/
src/
build.ts
install-plugin.sh
.github/
